[center][size=6][b]Hollowfang[/b][/size]
[i]A dagger that grows with you, and with every life it takes.[/i][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]About[/b][/size]

Hollowfang is a unique Elven dagger that stays useful for your whole playthrough. It starts as a modest, steel-tier blade, keeps pace with the best daggers as you level, and gains new abilities from the lives it takes.

It's never the strongest weapon in the room. It's a weapon you can carry from Helgen to the end of the game, and it picks up a few tricks along the way.

[line]

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Yours from the start.[/b] Hollowfang appears in your inventory as soon as the mod loads, in a new game or an existing save.
[*][b]Scales with your level.[/b] Its damage keeps pace with the best dagger tier you'd otherwise be carrying, from steel up to daedric.
[*][b]Smithing-friendly.[/b] Improve it at any grindstone. The Elven Smithing perk applies.
[*][b]Absorb Stamina enchantment[/b], with a 1000-point charge.
[*][b]Grows with every kill.[/b] Kills made with Hollowfang unlock new abilities.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Level scaling[/b][/size]

Hollowfang's damage multiplier rises with your character level:

[list]
[*]Level 1–11: steel tier (×1.00)
[*]Level 12–23: elven tier (×1.15)
[*]Level 24–35: glass tier (×1.30)
[*]Level 36–45: ebony tier (×1.45)
[*]Level 46+: daedric tier (×1.60)
[/list]

The scaling only keeps Hollowfang level with normal gear; it doesn't add power on top. One-Handed perks, sneak attacks and Smithing improvements apply exactly as they would to any other dagger.

[line]

[size=4][b]Kill unlocks[/b][/size]

Hollowfang counts every creature or person you kill with it. Hitting corpses doesn't count.

[list]
[*][b]Stride (every 10 kills):[/b] +2% movement speed per tier, up to +10% at 50 kills.
[*][b]Soul Feeding (10 kills):[/b] each kill restores some of the enchantment's charge, so Hollowfang feeds itself.
[/list]

All bonuses only apply while Hollowfang is equipped. More unlocks are planned for future updates.

[line]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Skyrim Special Edition or Anniversary Edition
[*]No SKSE or other dependencies
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[b]Vortex (recommended):[/b] click [i]Mod Manager Download[/i], then enable and deploy the mod.

[b]Manual:[/b] extract the archive into your [i]Skyrim Special Edition\Data[/i] folder and enable [i]Hollowfang.esp[/i] in your load order.

[line]

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]

Hollowfang only adds new records and doesn't change anything in the base game, so it should be compatible with any other mod. Load order doesn't matter.

[b]Uninstalling:[/b] as with any scripted mod, don't remove Hollowfang partway through a playthrough. Its scripts leave data in your save that can't be cleanly removed.

[line]

[size=4][b]FAQ[/b][/size]

[b]Where do I find the dagger?[/b]
It's added to your inventory automatically when the mod first loads. You'll see the message "Something cold settles into your pack."

[b]Does it work with my existing save?[/b]
Yes. Load your save, and the dagger arrives within a few seconds.

[b]Isn't a free unique dagger at level 1 overpowered?[/b]
It starts at steel tier, so you'll still find better weapons early on. It only catches up with them as you level, and never goes beyond them.

[b]Does it need SKSE?[/b]
No. Hollowfang uses only the base game's own systems.

[line]

[size=4][b]Known issues[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Version 1.0.0 shows a "Hollowfang controller loaded" debug notification when the mod first loads. This will be removed in 1.0.1.
[/list]

Found a bug? Please report it in the Bugs tab, and include your game version and any other mods that affect weapons or perks.

[line]

